# Code owners for the paths that still need the owner to merge them.
#
# GitHub no longer requires code-owner review here: the ruleset
# (.github/rulesets/main.json) sets require_code_owner_review to false, by the
# owner's decision of 2026-11-23. What makes these paths wait for the owner is
# the Hive's own merge gate, its human_merge_paths setting, which lists exactly
# these paths for this repository: the Hive labels a pull request that touches
# one of them `needs-owner-merge` and leaves it for a person to merge. That
# setting lives on the Hive, not in this repository.
#
# This file only makes GitHub ask the owner to review such a pull request. Every
# other change, Tier 3 or not, merges on the required check and the Hive's AI
# reviewer, with no owner review (see docs/branch-protection.md).
#
# tests/test_codeowners.py fails if this list stops being exactly these paths,
# if a catch-all `*` line comes back, or if a line owns a file the
# area/safety-critical label in .github/labeler.yml does not cover.

# Image signing: the public key, the signing and promotion code, the policy the
# image installs to verify signatures, the action that installs the cosign
# binary the signing key is handed to (#177, option B), and the action that
# pushes the image that is then signed.
/cosign.pub                                                   @Danathar
/ci_tools/sign_image.py                                       @Danathar
/ci_tools/promote_stable.py                                   @Danathar
/files/scripts/configure_signing_policy.py                    @Danathar
/.github/actions/install-signing-tools/                       @Danathar
/.github/actions/publish-native-image/                        @Danathar

# Every workflow, not only build.yml. The production-signing environment has a
# branch policy but no required reviewer, so any workflow on main can ask for it
# and be handed the cosign key. That makes every workflow part of the signing
# path.
/.github/workflows/                                           @Danathar

# What keeps main behind a pull request, and this file.
/.github/rulesets/                                            @Danathar
/.github/CODEOWNERS                                           @Danathar
